  "scope": "Tiers 1, 2 and 3: production decode_value on Linux x86-64, every finite input slice and DecodeLimits; rejection maps to None, accepted values satisfy wf and exact canonical encoding, and input length is bounded. Effective depth is min(requested depth, 1024). T4 invokes encode_value_with_limits for representation-valid Value storage under wf and output-prefix length plus spec_encode length <= usize::MAX. T5 proves spec_decode completeness by structural node-count induction and carries it through production correspondence: wf(value, limits) and spec_encode(value).len() <= limits.max_input_bytes imply Ok with model value. The production round trip retains both byte bounds. Standard allocation and execution assumptions apply.",
